<pre class="poem">

<b>AM Radio Abecedarian</b>
At the early hours of the morning
Barely awake my ears are greeted to the sound of static that
Cracks through the old speakers of the Buick Lesabre

Don’t doubt this fact:
Every self respecting North Jersey man 
Finds comfort in the waves of
Gravelly voices griping over contests they have no control of.

Hank from Hackensack
Is certain that 
Jazz should ride the bench for 
Kicking the ball off his foot while a 
Lollipop hung from his mouth

Matt from Monmouth
Never has seen such
Obscene play from the starting 
Power forward for the Knickerbockers 

Quintessential is the art of the complaint here.
Rarely is there anything of merit
Spit out over the speaker.

Too often the pundits repeat and reword 
Utilizing every corner of
Vocabulary possible to keep dials tuned to 

WFAN New York, to most the
Xeric of the broadcasting world.
Yet for me, on hot and humid May mornings, it is the
Zenith of talk radio.
